  <page_number>86</page_number>
  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Raptásque stupris polluit insolens</i></p>
    <l><i>Hostis maritas, virginésque:</i></l>
    <l><i>Non scelere abstinuit nefando.</i></l>
    <p><i>Quod magna summi dextera vindicis</i></p>
    <l><i>Frata prisco tempore punijt</i></l>
    <l><i>Quum vertit infames Sodomas</i></l>
    <l><i>Æthereum iaculata sulphur.</i></l>
    <p><i>Quas pleniori copia fuderat</i></p>
    <l><i>Per arua cornu largáque faustitas</i></l>
    <l><i>Fruges &amp; vndantis Lyæi</i></l>
    <l><i>Dona ferox sibi vindicauit.</i></l>
    <p><i>Boum labores perdidit &amp; sata</i></p>
    <l><i>Flammisque pagos subiciens vagis</i></l>
    <l><i>Incendit &amp; semen paratum</i></l>
    <l><i>Credere humo vetuit feraci.</i></l>
    <p><i>Quæ dixit atrox, Versoui simul</i></p>
    <l><i>Vallauit arces: tuta nec amplius</i></l>
    <l><i>Nauis per obsessi Lemanni</i></l>
    <l><i>Cærule as volitauit vndas!</i></l>
    <p><i>Geneua vitias esurie manus</i></p>
    <l><i>Nunc tendet exspes: libera nunc iugo</i></l>
    <l><i>Subdet Sabaudo colla, nostris</i></l>
    <l><i>Seruiet imperiys subasta.</i></l>
    <p><i>Cœli sed alto vertice qui sedet</i></p>
    <l><i>Orbémque iustis arbitriis regit</i></l>
    <l><i>Iras Tyranni tam cruentas</i></l>
    <l><i>Spésq; trucésque minas repressit.</i></l>
    <p><i>Quum rebus arctis impauidum tibi</i></p>
    <l><i>Geneua</i></l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "Geneua" at lower right is a catchword and is placed in the text as printed. Long s rendered as plain s; some letters in the scan are worn (e.g. "vitias", "Lemanni") and read as printed as far as legible.</notes>
